.TH SECONDTAKE 1 "2026-11-27" "secondtake 0.1.0" "Retrospective Line"
.SH NAME
secondtake \- matched before-and-after evaluator for agent setup changes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B secondtake compare
.I before_dir after_dir
.B \-\-registration
.I registration.json
.RI [ "\-\-judge " fixture.json|live ]
.RI [ "\-o " comparison.json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B secondtake
pairs before-and-after directories of
.B flighttape 1.0
session tapes by Canonical Form 1 task key, scores each matched pair on
four measures (token cost, wall duration, redo rework moments, and error
rescue rate) against margins in
.IR registration.json ,
and emits a deterministic
.BR keep ,
.BR tune ,
.BR revert ,
or
.B abstain
proposal JSON document.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-\-registration " "FILE"
Pre-registered change and margin declaration JSON file (required).
.TP
.BI "\-\-judge " "SOURCE"
Replay judgments JSON file or literal
.B live
(invoking
.B JEV_CALL
in the 1-regression tradeoff band).
.TP
.BI "\-o, \-\-output " "FILE"
Write the comparison JSON document atomically to FILE.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B JEV_CALL
Executable or Python connector consulted when
.B \-\-judge live
enters the 1-regression band.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Comparison succeeded and JSON report was emitted.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid registration, unreadable directory, judge error, or I/O refusal.
.TP
.B 2
Command-line usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
secondtake compare examples/before examples/after \
  --registration examples/registration.json
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/david-engelmann/secondtake
